rs older The Adams  Family Values scene marked the latter  actors first on-screen kiss as well in a  1993 interview Richie was asked if there  was a big to do made about the kiss she  brushed it off saying no there was no  real big deal about it because I mean  when you think about it there's so much  of that you know in movies and  everything and it's just a movie in a  way it's a little sad that Richie had to  grow up quite so fast and in the  Limelight while she may have told the  interviewer that it was no big deal  krumholtz told BuzzFeed for the film's  20th anniversary that Richie was less  than thrilled with her scene partner's  peach fuzz he noted that made me really  self-conscious  most child stars have done anything  humanly possible to distance themselves  from their most iconic role but  Christina Ricci has other ideas she told  the AV club that The Adams Family films  have had the biggest impact on her  career and life she remains fully aware  of the role that defined her career and  still feels a kinship toward her darker  Alter Ego I just got to do a lot of  weird things that you know normally I  wouldn't get to do Richie told the AV  club I feel very inextricably bound to  Wednesday we'll probably never know just  how much the role-shaped Richie as a  person but she certainly defied the  tragic fate of many child stars so maybe  Wednesday's resilience and strength  played a part in Richie's transition  from a child star to a successful adult  actress she posed this question to the  AV club it's like a chicken or egg  debate did I influence her as a  character or did she as a character  influence my personality in a sobering  follow-up thought Richie noted the way  memory Works in childhood it all blurs  so I don't have a sense of who I was or  what I felt felt like before I was an  actress essentially so in a way she and  Wednesday are permanently intertwined  For Better or For Worse  if you thought young Wednesday Adams is  a mood she has nothing 