n according to  a conversation Ortega had with ew that  was one of the biggest challenges of  taking on the role Ortega explained to  the outlet we've never seen her as a  teenage girl you know it's funny and  sweet and almost Charming to hear this  eight-year-old's obsession with murder  and blood and guts as she gets older  that nasty attitude or those biting  remarks it's almost kind of hard to not  make it sound like every other teenage  girl it's tough to film such a long  series about a sardonic and somewhat  unemotional character but Tim Burton  knows what he's doing Ortega praise to  Burton's attention to detail to ew  saying that has been really incredible  just being such a fan of his work prior  but also getting to know him and  realizing he's the most detail-oriented  director I'll ever work with though  Ortega noted some of the challenges she  had getting into character and keeping  Wednesday fresh Christina Ricci isn't  worried about the younger star's  performance as it turns out Adam's  Family Values won't be the last time  fancy Richie in this kooky World her  role in Wednesday has given her a front  row seat for Ortega's performance and  according to Richie she's living up to  the hype after applauding Tim Burton and  Gwendolyn Christie's work on the show  during a variety interview Ricci deemed  Ortega's performance as Wednesday  incredible Richie told the outlet I saw  some of the Wardrobe photos before I  went to set so I knew what she looked  like in character and I was like it's  such a great modern take on Wednesday  it's so true totally to the heart and  soul of the original but it's also  incredibly modern and it's great if  Richie is down with Ortega his take on  the character fans have gotten all the  approval they need directly from a  generation's favorite on-screen  Wednesday  [Music]

